  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Find all triangles with area $\\sqrt{2}$ and two sides of length $2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Two triangles: the included angle is $45^\\circ$ or $135^\\circ$.\n\nUse the area rule and $\\sin(180^\\circ-C)=\\sin C$.",
      "worked": "Let $C$ be the angle between the two sides of length $2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{2}&=\\frac12(2)(2)\\sin C\\\\\\sin C&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\\\C&=45^\\circ\\text{ or }135^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$\nThe two triangles have sides $2$ and $2$ with included angle $45^\\circ$ or $135^\\circ$, since $\\sin135^\\circ=\\sin45^\\circ$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
